{%- comment -%}
  Senseless — sitewide structured data (JSON-LD), GEO/SEO layer.
  Rendered once from layout/theme.liquid <head>.

  ONE @graph per page, @id-linked. Before this rewrite the theme emitted 3–4 free-standing
  JSON-LD documents per page with no relationship between them: Organization existed only on
  the homepage and on 2 of 32 /pages/*, and no page type emitted a WebPage node at all — so an
  answer engine reading a collection or a guide had no path from the page it was reading back to
  the company that publishes it. The entity graph, not schema coverage, was the gap.

  Node addresses (stable, dereferenceable, reused by every other emitter on the page):
    {shop.url}/#organization        the company  — full detail, emitted on EVERY page type
    {shop.url}/#website             the site     — publisher -> #organization
    {canonical_url}#webpage         this page    — isPartOf -> #website, about -> #organization
    {canonical_url}#breadcrumb      this trail   — referenced by #webpage.breadcrumb
    {canonical_url}#product         this product — mainEntity of #webpage (product pages). A Product,
                                    except on the BASE URL of a two-size product, where it is a
                                    ProductGroup whose sizes are nested in hasVariant at
                                    {canonical_url}#variant-<variant id> (never top-level nodes)
    {canonical_url}#itemlist        this list    — mainEntity of #webpage (collection pages)

  Other emitters that join this graph by @id rather than duplicating it:
    sections/senseless-faq-accordion.liquid  FAQPage       (its own document — Google reads
                                                            FAQPage standalone; left alone)
    sections/senseless-article.liquid        Article       -> isPartOf #webpage, #breadcrumb
    sections/senseless-page-schema.liquid    AboutPage / ContactPage — adds that @type to #webpage
                                                            by re-declaring the same @id (type only);
                                                            Service — its own #service node
    sections/senseless-org-schema.liquid     now emits nothing; #organization is sitewide

  All strings go through the `json` filter, which quotes and escapes — the output is valid JSON
  by construction. Free text that can carry HTML entities (page_title / page_description, which
  Shopify pre-escapes, and anything through strip_html) goes through snippets/senseless-jsonld-text
  first, because JSON-LD is not HTML-parsed and Google reads "&amp;" literally. Prices,
  availability and currency come from live product data. The seller is the parent company,
  Matrix Health Group Ltd.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign base = shop.url
  assign seller_name = 'Senseless'
  assign seller_legal = 'Matrix Health Group Ltd'
  comment
    VAT identification number (ECR 2002 reg 6(1)(g)). Unspaced with the GB national prefix per the
    schema.org vatID convention — the visible surfaces (footer, contact, llms.txt) use the spaced
    human form "GB 523 781 682". That divergence is deliberate; don't "align" them.
  endcomment
  assign seller_vat = 'GB523781682'
  assign cur = cart.currency.iso_code | default: shop.currency

  assign page_url = canonical_url | default: base
  assign org_id = base | append: '/#organization'
  assign site_id = base | append: '/#website'
  assign webpage_id = page_url | append: '#webpage'
  assign crumb_id = page_url | append: '#breadcrumb'

  # Shipping + return policy node addresses. Sitewide-stable (they are the same policy on every
  # page) and absolute like every other @id in this graph. The shipping nodes are emitted only on
  # product + collection pages, the only page types that carry an Offer to reference them; the
  # return policy is nested in #organization, so it is on every page.
  assign ship_standard_id = base | append: '/#shipping-standard'
  assign ship_express_id = base | append: '/#shipping-express'
  assign ship_next_id = base | append: '/#shipping-next-working-day'
  assign ship_standard_free_id = base | append: '/#shipping-standard-free'
  assign ship_next_free_id = base | append: '/#shipping-next-working-day-free'
  assign return_id = base | append: '/#return-policy'

  # Same-day dispatch cut-off, shared by every shipping method. 15:00 local (was 15:30 from 23 Aug
  # to 12 Sep 2026, and 13:00 before that). cutoffTime must be ISO 8601 WITH a timezone offset (valid schema.org on an
  # offer-level ShippingDeliveryTime; Google documents it for organisation-level ShippingService, so it may ignore it here), and a hardcoded
  # one would be wrong for half the year -- '+01:00' reads as 14:00 GMT once BST ends. So the
  # offset is taken from the STORE's own clock via `date: '%z'` (Shopify renders this in the shop
  # timezone, Europe/London), which yields +0100 in summer and +0000 in winter and needs no
  # seasonal edit. Built from %z rather than %:z because %z is the safely-supported form; the
  # colon is inserted here to give the +HH:MM shape Google's examples use.
  assign tz_h = 'now' | date: '%z' | slice: 0, 3
  assign tz_m = 'now' | date: '%z' | slice: 3, 2
  assign dispatch_cutoff = '15:00:00' | append: tz_h | append: ':' | append: tz_m

  # NO Offer.priceValidUntil, on purpose. It went out on 23 Sep 2026 (31 Dec of next year) and came
  # off the same evening: Google's Rich Results Test then flagged a NEW non-critical Merchant
  # listings issue on every Offer, 'Missing field "validFrom"', because Google now reads
  # priceValidUntil as the END OF A SALE and asks for its start. Search Console had shown 0
  # Merchant listings issues and never flagged priceValidUntil as missing, so it bought nothing.
  # Only add it with a real sale window (validFrom + priceValidUntil on a StrikethroughPrice offer).

  # WebPage @type, specialised per page type. senseless-page-schema.liquid re-declares
  # #webpage as AboutPage/ContactPage on the two templates that need it.
  assign webpage_type = 'WebPage'
  assign crumb_type = ''
  case request.page_type
    when 'product'
      assign webpage_type = 'ItemPage'
      assign crumb_type = 'product'
    when 'collection'
      assign webpage_type = 'CollectionPage'
      assign crumb_type = 'collection'
    when 'page'
      assign crumb_type = 'page'
    when 'blog'
      assign webpage_type = 'CollectionPage'
    when 'search'
      assign webpage_type = 'SearchResultsPage'
  endcase

  # Page name + description, best available source per page type.
  # 1200, not 300 — the same reasoning that lifted the Product node's cap on 6 Aug. At 300 a
  # collection description was cut mid-sentence, so the text an answer engine reads lost the
  # part that distinguishes one collection from the next. Where a collection has no body the
  # admin SEO description stands in, which is why page_description is the base assignment.
  assign sd_name = page_title | default: shop.name
  assign sd_desc = page_description
  case request.page_type
    when 'product'
      assign sd_name = product.title
      assign sd_desc = product.description | strip_html | strip_newlines
    when 'collection'
      assign sd_name = collection.title
      if collection.description != blank
        assign sd_desc = collection.description | strip_html | strip_newlines
      endif
    when 'article'
      assign sd_name = article.title
  endcase
  # Decode entities before truncating, so the cap counts real characters and can't cut one in half.
  capture sd_name
    render 'senseless-jsonld-text', text: sd_name
  endcapture
  capture sd_desc
    render 'senseless-jsonld-text', text: sd_desc
  endcapture
  assign sd_desc = sd_desc | truncate: 1200

  # Dates. `updated_at` is not documented on the Liquid page/article objects; if it resolves it is
  # used, and if it does not the `default` filter falls back to the publish date. Either way the
  # emitted value is a real date from Shopify, never a rendered-at timestamp.
  assign sd_published = ''
  assign sd_modified = ''
  if request.page_type == 'article'
    assign sd_published = article.published_at | date: '%Y-%m-%d'
    assign sd_modified = article.updated_at | default: article.published_at | date: '%Y-%m-%d'
  elsif request.page_type == 'page'
    assign sd_published = page.published_at | date: '%Y-%m-%d'
    assign sd_modified = page.updated_at | default: page.published_at | date: '%Y-%m-%d'
  endif

  # Social profiles for sameAs. No Senseless profile exists yet (2026-08-13) — the settings are
  # here so the entity graph gains them the day one does, without another theme change.
  assign sd_same_as = ''
  if settings.social_instagram_link != blank
    assign sd_same_as = sd_same_as | append: settings.social_instagram_link | append: '|'
  endif
  if settings.social_tiktok_link != blank
    assign sd_same_as = sd_same_as | append: settings.social_tiktok_link | append: '|'
  endif
  if settings.social_facebook_link != blank
    assign sd_same_as = sd_same_as | append: settings.social_facebook_link | append: '|'
  endif
  if settings.social_youtube_link != blank
    assign sd_same_as = sd_same_as | append: settings.social_youtube_link | append: '|'
  endif
  assign sd_same_as = sd_same_as | split: '|'
-%}
<script type="application/ld+json" class="jdgm-server-jld">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {%- comment -%}
      OnlineStore: Google recommends the most specific Organization subtype ("if you have an
      ecommerce site ... the OnlineStore subtype"). "Organization" stays in the array so anything
      matching the plain type still finds it; every { "@id": #organization } reference is unchanged.
      The return policy is nested here (hasMerchantReturnPolicy, @id #return-policy) so it is on
      every page, including the homepage; every Offer still references it by @id. Nested, not a bare
      { "@id" }, because a bare reference would be an empty policy on pages that don't define it.
      Moved here 23 Sep 2026 with unchanged terms (it was a separate node on product and collection
      pages only). If the returns wording changes, update it here.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {
      "@type": ["Organization", "OnlineStore"],
      "@id": {{ org_id | json }},
      "name": {{ seller_name | json }},
      "legalName": {{ seller_legal | json }},
      "vatID": {{ seller_vat | json }},
      "url": {{ base | append: '/' | json }},
      "logo": {
        "@type": "ImageObject",
        "@id": {{ base | append: '/#logo' | json }},
        "url": {{ 'senseless-logo.png' | asset_url | prepend: 'https:' | json }},
        "caption": {{ seller_name | json }}
      },
      "image": { "@id": {{ base | append: '/#logo' | json }} },
      "address": {
        "@type": "PostalAddress",
        "streetAddress": "Paddock Business Centre, 2 Paddock Road",
        "addressLocality": "Skelmersdale",
        "postalCode": "WN8 9PL",
        "addressCountry": "GB"
      },
      "telephone": "+443330495549",
      "email": "cs@senseless.uk",
      "areaServed": "GB",
      {%- if sd_same_as.size > 0 -%}
      "sameAs": [
        {%- for profile in sd_same_as -%}{{ profile | json }}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}{%- endfor -%}
      ],
      {%- endif -%}
      "contactPoint": [{
        "@type": "ContactPoint",
        "telephone": "+443330495549",
        "email": "cs@senseless.uk",
        "contactType": "customer service",
        "areaServed": "GB",
        "availableLanguage": "English"
      }],
      "hasMerchantReturnPolicy": {
        "@type": "MerchantReturnPolicy",
        "@id": {{ return_id | json }},
        "applicableCountry": "GB",
        "returnPolicyCategory": "https://schema.org/MerchantReturnFiniteReturnWindow",
        "merchantReturnDays": 30,
        "returnMethod": "https://schema.org/ReturnByMail",
        "returnFees": "https://schema.org/ReturnFeesCustomerResponsibility"
      },
      "brand": { "@type": "Brand", "name": {{ seller_name | json }} }
    },
    {
      "@type": "WebSite",
      "@id": {{ site_id | json }},
      "name": {{ seller_name | json }},
      "url": {{ base | append: '/' | json }},
      "inLanguage": "en-GB",
      "publisher": { "@id": {{ org_id | json }} },
      "potentialAction": {
        "@type": "SearchAction",
        "target": { "@type": "EntryPoint", "urlTemplate": "{{ base }}/search?q={search_term_string}" },
        "query-input": "required name=search_term_string"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": {{ webpage_type | json }},
      "@id": {{ webpage_id | json }},
      "url": {{ page_url | json }},
      "name": {{ sd_name | json }},
      {%- if sd_desc != blank -%}"description": {{ sd_desc | json }},{%- endif -%}
      {%- if sd_published != blank -%}"datePublished": {{ sd_published | json }},{%- endif -%}
      {%- if sd_modified != blank -%}"dateModified": {{ sd_modified | json }},{%- endif -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Articles get the breadcrumb reference but not the node: sections/senseless-article.liquid
        emits the BreadcrumbList itself at the same #breadcrumb address, so pointing at it here
        links the two without putting a second trail on the page.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if crumb_type != blank or request.page_type == 'article' -%}"breadcrumb": { "@id": {{ crumb_id | json }} },{%- endif -%}
      {%- if request.page_type == 'product' -%}"mainEntity": { "@id": {{ page_url | append: '#product' | json }} },{%- endif -%}
      {%- if request.page_type == 'collection' -%}"mainEntity": { "@id": {{ page_url | append: '#itemlist' | json }} },{%- endif -%}
      {%- if request.page_type == 'article' -%}"mainEntity": { "@id": {{ page_url | append: '#article' | json }} },{%- endif -%}
      "isPartOf": { "@id": {{ site_id | json }} },
      "about": { "@id": {{ org_id | json }} },
      "publisher": { "@id": {{ org_id | json }} },
      "inLanguage": "en-GB"
    }
    {%- if crumb_type != blank -%},
      {%- render 'senseless-breadcrumbs-jsonld', base: base, crumb_id: crumb_id, crumb_type: crumb_type -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if request.page_type == 'product' or request.page_type == 'collection' -%},
    {%- comment -%}
      Shipping + return policy, defined ONCE per page and referenced by @id from every offer.
      (Since 23 Sep 2026 the return policy node lives inside #organization, above, so it is
      emitted on every page; the five shipping nodes below are still product + collection only.)

      Google documents this exact pattern (search/docs/appearance/structured-data/product-variants):
      an offer may carry "shippingDetails": { "@id": "#..." } and "hasMerchantReturnPolicy":
      { "@id": "#..." } as long as the node itself is present in the same JSON-LD document. Before
      this, the five shipping blocks and the return policy were written out inline inside the
      product offer loop and NOT written at all on collection pages — so every Product nested in a
      collection ItemList was missing hasMerchantReturnPolicy and shippingDetails, which is what
      Search Console reported on 19 Aug 2026 as three Merchant listings issues across the 19
      collection URLs. Referencing rather than repeating fixes the collections, removes the
      per-variant duplication on PDPs, and leaves the rate card in exactly one place in this file.

      These five entries mirror the LIVE Shopify rate card for the GB zone exactly,
      re-read from the Admin API on 2026-08-14 (deliveryProfiles -> methodDefinitions); method names
      re-read 2026-09-12 after the rename to "Next Working Day (Order by 3pm)", prices and conditions unchanged:

        Standard 4-6 Working Days        GBP 1.99   0      - 39.99
        Express 2-3 working days         GBP 3.99   0      - 79.99
        Next Working Day (Order by 3pm)  GBP 8.99   0      - 79.99
        Standard 4-6 Working Days        GBP 0.00   40.00  - 79.99
        Next Working Day (Order by 3pm)  GBP 0.00   80.00  +

      CORRECTION, and it matters. On 14 Aug this block was briefly cut down to two free options,
      on the reasoning that the 1.99 rate and the 4-6 day transit "appear nowhere in published
      copy" and that 4-6 days "contradicts next-day delivery". Both halves were wrong. 1.99 / 4-6
      days IS the real sub-40 standard method, and it does not contradict next-day because they
      are different methods a customer chooses between. The error was treating the policy PAGES as
      the source of truth for shipping when the rate card is -- and the policy pages are themselves
      incomplete, since neither of them mentions Express at all. Accurate structured data was
      deleted on a false premise; that restored it from the authoritative source.

      WHICH nodes an offer references depends on its price: snippets/senseless-shipping-refs.liquid
      picks the methods valid for that item bought on its own (22 Sep 2026, study V17). The order-value
      bands used to sit here as eligibleTransactionVolume. schema.org doesn't allow that on
      OfferShippingDetails, so Google read the two £0 nodes as applying to every offer. The nodes
      now carry no band; the per-offer selection does the job, and Merchant Center's own shipping
      settings (account level) remain what Shopping ads use.

      handlingTime is 0-1 day on every method: ordered before 15:00 on a working day it is
      dispatched the same day, otherwise the next working day. Keep this in step with the
      rate card -- if shipping changes in Shopify, change it here too.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {
      "@type": "OfferShippingDetails",
      "@id": {{ ship_standard_id | json }},
      "name": "Standard delivery",
      "shippingRate": { "@type": "MonetaryAmount", "value": "1.99", "currency": "GBP" },
      "shippingDestination": { "@type": "DefinedRegion", "addressCountry": "GB" },
      "deliveryTime": {
        "@type": "ShippingDeliveryTime",
        "cutoffTime": {{ dispatch_cutoff | json }},
        "handlingTime": { "@type": "QuantitativeValue", "minValue": 0, "maxValue": 1, "unitCode": "DAY" },
        "transitTime": { "@type": "QuantitativeValue", "minValue": 4, "maxValue": 6, "unitCode": "DAY" }
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "OfferShippingDetails",
      "@id": {{ ship_express_id | json }},
      "name": "Express delivery",
      "shippingRate": { "@type": "MonetaryAmount", "value": "3.99", "currency": "GBP" },
      "shippingDestination": { "@type": "DefinedRegion", "addressCountry": "GB" },
      "deliveryTime": {
        "@type": "ShippingDeliveryTime",
        "cutoffTime": {{ dispatch_cutoff | json }},
        "handlingTime": { "@type": "QuantitativeValue", "minValue": 0, "maxValue": 1, "unitCode": "DAY" },
        "transitTime": { "@type": "QuantitativeValue", "minValue": 2, "maxValue": 3, "unitCode": "DAY" }
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "OfferShippingDetails",
      "@id": {{ ship_next_id | json }},
      "name": "Next working day",
      "shippingRate": { "@type": "MonetaryAmount", "value": "8.99", "currency": "GBP" },
      "shippingDestination": { "@type": "DefinedRegion", "addressCountry": "GB" },
      "deliveryTime": {
        "@type": "ShippingDeliveryTime",
        "cutoffTime": {{ dispatch_cutoff | json }},
        "handlingTime": { "@type": "QuantitativeValue", "minValue": 0, "maxValue": 1, "unitCode": "DAY" },
        "transitTime": { "@type": "QuantitativeValue", "minValue": 1, "maxValue": 1, "unitCode": "DAY" }
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "OfferShippingDetails",
      "@id": {{ ship_standard_free_id | json }},
      "name": "Free standard delivery on orders from GBP 40",
      "shippingRate": { "@type": "MonetaryAmount", "value": "0", "currency": "GBP" },
      "shippingDestination": { "@type": "DefinedRegion", "addressCountry": "GB" },
      "deliveryTime": {
        "@type": "ShippingDeliveryTime",
        "cutoffTime": {{ dispatch_cutoff | json }},
        "handlingTime": { "@type": "QuantitativeValue", "minValue": 0, "maxValue": 1, "unitCode": "DAY" },
        "transitTime": { "@type": "QuantitativeValue", "minValue": 4, "maxValue": 6, "unitCode": "DAY" }
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "OfferShippingDetails",
      "@id": {{ ship_next_free_id | json }},
      "name": "Free next working day on orders from GBP 80",
      "shippingRate": { "@type": "MonetaryAmount", "value": "0", "currency": "GBP" },
      "shippingDestination": { "@type": "DefinedRegion", "addressCountry": "GB" },
      "deliveryTime": {
        "@type": "ShippingDeliveryTime",
        "cutoffTime": {{ dispatch_cutoff | json }},
        "handlingTime": { "@type": "QuantitativeValue", "minValue": 0, "maxValue": 1, "unitCode": "DAY" },
        "transitTime": { "@type": "QuantitativeValue", "minValue": 1, "maxValue": 1, "unitCode": "DAY" }
      }
    }
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- case request.page_type -%}

    {%- when 'product' -%},
      {%- comment -%}
        1200, not 480. At 480 every strength SKU's description was cut mid-sentence with an ellipsis, so the
        text Google and the answer engines read lost the sizes and the "Formulated in the UK, CPSR assessed"
        credential — and, before the copy was restructured, the "not a medicine" classification too. Product
        schema has no strict length limit and the Merchant Center feed already takes the body whole, so this
        aligns the two ad-facing surfaces. The cap stays as a guard against an oversized paste.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign pd = product.description | strip_html | strip_newlines
        capture pd
          render 'senseless-jsonld-text', text: pd
        endcapture
        assign pd = pd | truncate: 1200
        if pd == blank
          assign pd = product.title | append: ' — a topical cosmetic preparation by Senseless.'
        endif
        assign v1 = product.selected_or_first_available_variant | default: product.variants.first
        comment
          Judge.me rating, synced to the reviews.* metafields. rating is a `rating`-type metafield
          → its .value is a Rating object whose .value is the number. rating_count is a plain
          integer. aggregateRating is emitted ONLY when there are reviews (count > 0) — kits and
          no-review products have null metafields and emit nothing, because an empty or zero
          aggregateRating is a Rich Results error. Rating object only; no review text.
        endcomment
        assign ss_rating = product.metafields.reviews.rating.value
        assign ss_rcount = product.metafields.reviews.rating_count.value

        comment
          ProductGroup gate. ss_group is true on ONE kind of page only: the BASE product URL (no
          ?variant=) of a product with more than one variant and a single option named "Size".
          Today that is the 5 two-size PDPs (Clinical + Advanced cream 10g/30g; Clinical, Advanced +
          Professional gel 15ml/35ml). Every other page takes the one-Offer Product in the else
          branch, whose output is unchanged: every ?variant= URL (the Merchant Center landing pages)
          and all 12 single-variant products.
          - variants.size, NOT has_only_default_variant: the 3 sprays, the cleanser and Professional
            cream have a one-value "Size" option, so has_only_default_variant is false for them.
          - product.selected_variant is nil unless the URL carries ?variant=<id> (shopify.dev: "If no
            variant is currently selected, then nil is returned."). If Shopify ever sets it some other
            way, the page falls back to the one-Offer Product, which is the Merchant Center-safe side.
          - A second option, or an option renamed away from "Size", also falls back (and the larger
            size disappears from Search again) until variesBy is mapped for it here.
        endcomment
        assign ss_group = false
        if product.variants.size > 1 and product.options_with_values.size == 1
          assign ss_opt_name = product.options_with_values.first.name | downcase | strip
          if ss_opt_name == 'size'
            unless product.selected_variant
              assign ss_group = true
            endunless
          endif
        endif
      -%}
      {%- if ss_group -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        ProductGroup: base URL of a two-size product only (gate above). Google's single-page variant
        pattern (developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/structured-data/product-variants): one
        group at the canonical URL (every ?variant= URL canonicalises here), each size a Product
        nested in hasVariant with ONE Offer whose url is that size's own ?variant= URL. Until this
        change the base URL carried only the first size, so the larger sizes (price, SKU, GTIN) were
        invisible to Search.

        Why the group is NOT on ?variant= URLs (DECISIONS-LOG 22 Sep Decision 6, a511a95): those are
        the pages Merchant Center compares prices on, and it matches markup to a feed item only if
        "There's a single offer on the landing page" or every offer's SKU/GTIN equals the item's
        (support.google.com/merchants/answer/7331077). Moving the group there is a separate decision
        (needs every size's feed gtin = its gtin13, checked in Merchant Center first).

        Judge.me (bundle judgeme-762): its review widget's V() rewrites the @id of any TOP-LEVEL node
        typed Product in this class-marked script whose @id is not canonical#product. So: @type is
        exactly "ProductGroup" (never an array containing "Product"), the @id stays #product, and the
        sizes stay NESTED in hasVariant. Never hoist them to @graph siblings.

        Also: aggregateRating on the group only (Judge.me reviews are per product; Google: "representative
        of all variants"); sku / mpn / gtin13 on each size, never the group; the size this page
        preselects (v1) is listed first; each size's shipping refs come from ITS price. The Offer body
        mirrors the one-Offer Product's below with v for v1 -- change one, change both. Size names are
        Shopify's own ("<title> - <size>"); no new copy.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {
        "@type": "ProductGroup",
        "@id": {{ page_url | append: '#product' | json }},
        "name": {{ product.title | json }},
        "description": {{ pd | json }},
        "url": {{ base | append: product.url | json }},
        "mainEntityOfPage": { "@id": {{ webpage_id | json }} },
        {%- if product.images.size > 0 -%}
        "image": [
          {%- for image in product.images limit: 5 -%}
            {{ image | image_url: width: 1200 | prepend: 'https:' | json }}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        ],
        {%- endif -%}
        "productGroupID": {{ product.id | append: '' | json }},
        "variesBy": ["https://schema.org/size"],
        "productID": {{ product.id | prepend: 'shopify_GB_' | json }},
        "identifier": [
          { "@type": "PropertyValue", "propertyID": "shopify_product_id", "value": {{ product.id | json }} }
        ],
        {%- if product.type != blank -%}"category": {{ product.type | json }},{%- endif -%}
        "brand": { "@type": "Brand", "name": {{ seller_name | json }} },
        "manufacturer": { "@id": {{ org_id | json }} },
        {%- if ss_rcount and ss_rcount > 0 and ss_rating != blank -%}
        "aggregateRating": {
          "@type": "AggregateRating",
          "ratingValue": "{{ ss_rating.rating }}",
          "reviewCount": "{{ ss_rcount }}",
          "bestRating": "5",
          "worstRating": "1"
        },
        {%- endif -%}
        "hasVariant": [
          {%- assign ss_sep = '' -%}
          {%- for ss_pass in (1..2) -%}
            {%- for v in product.variants -%}
              {%- if ss_pass == 1 and v.id != v1.id -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- if ss_pass == 2 and v.id == v1.id -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign ss_vimg = v.featured_image | default: product.featured_image -%}
              {{ ss_sep }}{
                "@type": "Product",
                "@id": {{ page_url | append: '#variant-' | append: v.id | json }},
                "name": {{ product.title | append: ' - ' | append: v.title | json }},
                "description": {{ pd | json }},
                {%- if ss_vimg -%}"image": {{ ss_vimg | image_url: width: 1200 | prepend: 'https:' | json }},{%- endif -%}
                {%- if v.sku != blank -%}
                "sku": {{ v.sku | json }},
                "mpn": {{ v.sku | json }},
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if v.barcode != blank -%}"gtin13": {{ v.barcode | json }},{%- endif -%}
                "size": {{ v.options.first | json }},
                "offers": {
                  "@type": "Offer",
                  {%- if v.sku != blank -%}"sku": {{ v.sku | json }},{%- endif -%}
                  {%- if v.barcode != blank -%}"gtin13": {{ v.barcode | json }},{%- endif -%}
                  {%- if v.title != 'Default Title' -%}"name": {{ v.title | json }},{%- endif -%}
                  "price": "{{ v.price | divided_by: 100.0 }}",
                  "priceCurrency": {{ cur | json }},
                  "itemCondition": "https://schema.org/NewCondition",
                  "availability": "https://schema.org/{% if v.available %}InStock{% else %}OutOfStock{% endif %}",
                  "url": {{ base | append: v.url | json }},
                  "seller": { "@id": {{ org_id | json }} },
                  "shippingDetails": {% render 'senseless-shipping-refs', price: v.price, std: ship_standard_id, express: ship_express_id, nwd: ship_next_id, std_free: ship_standard_free_id, nwd_free: ship_next_free_id %},
                  "hasMerchantReturnPolicy": { "@id": {{ return_id | json }} }
                }
              }
              {%- assign ss_sep = ',' -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        ]
      }
      {%- else -%}
      {
        "@type": "Product",
        "@id": {{ page_url | append: '#product' | json }},
        "name": {{ product.title | json }},
        "description": {{ pd | json }},
        "url": {{ base | append: product.url | json }},
        "mainEntityOfPage": { "@id": {{ webpage_id | json }} },
        {%- if product.images.size > 0 -%}
        "image": [
          {%- for image in product.images limit: 5 -%}
            {{ image | image_url: width: 1200 | prepend: 'https:' | json }}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        ],
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Product-level identifiers. Every SKU carries a Shopify SKU code. Since 23 Sep 2026 the GS1 UK
          code from the owner's "Barcodes" sheet is the barcode on 16 variants (DECISIONS-LOG 23 Sep
          Decision 5); VAD-4PK and the 5 kits have none, so gtin13 is emitted where it exists and never
          invented. productID is a label, 'shopify_GB_<numeric product id>', not a GID. The Google &
          YouTube feed keys its items as shopify_ZZ_<product id>_<variant id>, so this is not the MC
          item ID (study N30).
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if v1.sku != blank -%}
        "sku": {{ v1.sku | json }},
        "mpn": {{ v1.sku | json }},
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if v1.barcode != blank -%}"gtin13": {{ v1.barcode | json }},{%- endif -%}
        "productID": {{ product.id | prepend: 'shopify_GB_' | json }},
        "identifier": [
          { "@type": "PropertyValue", "propertyID": "shopify_product_id", "value": {{ product.id | json }} }
          {%- if v1.sku != blank -%},{ "@type": "PropertyValue", "propertyID": "sku", "value": {{ v1.sku | json }} }{%- endif -%}
        ],
        {%- if product.type != blank -%}"category": {{ product.type | json }},{%- endif -%}
        "brand": { "@type": "Brand", "name": {{ seller_name | json }} },
        "manufacturer": { "@id": {{ org_id | json }} },
        {%- if ss_rcount and ss_rcount > 0 and ss_rating != blank -%}
        "aggregateRating": {
          "@type": "AggregateRating",
          "ratingValue": "{{ ss_rating.rating }}",
          "reviewCount": "{{ ss_rcount }}",
          "bestRating": "5",
          "worstRating": "1"
        },
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          ONE Offer, for the SELECTED variant (the ?variant= on the URL, else the first available),
          so every attribute a crawler reads on a variant landing page (sku, gtin, price, url)
          belongs to the same size. Until 22 Sep 2026 this looped over every variant, with the
          smaller size first. Google Merchant Center's automatic updates then read the 15ml price
          (£24.99) on the Advanced Gel 35ml landing page and flagged "Mismatched product price"
          against the feed's £39.99. The other sizes are still reachable (the feed lists each
          variant's own ?variant= URL). Same fix as Totally Numb (21 Sep, 6457125).
          This node now renders on every ?variant= URL and every single-variant product; the base
          URL of a two-size product takes the ProductGroup above, which is how Search sees the other
          size. Keep this branch's OUTPUT unchanged: it is exactly what Merchant Center reads.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        "offers": [
          {
            "@type": "Offer",
            {%- if v1.sku != blank -%}"sku": {{ v1.sku | json }},{%- endif -%}
            {%- if v1.barcode != blank -%}"gtin13": {{ v1.barcode | json }},{%- endif -%}
            {%- if v1.title != 'Default Title' -%}"name": {{ v1.title | json }},{%- endif -%}
            "price": "{{ v1.price | divided_by: 100.0 }}",
            "priceCurrency": {{ cur | json }},
            "itemCondition": "https://schema.org/NewCondition",
            "availability": "https://schema.org/{% if v1.available %}InStock{% else %}OutOfStock{% endif %}",
            "url": {{ base | append: v1.url | json }},
            "seller": { "@id": {{ org_id | json }} },
            {%- comment -%}
              Shipping + return by reference. The nodes themselves are emitted once per page,
              above the page-type case — see the rate-card note there before changing anything.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            "shippingDetails": {% render 'senseless-shipping-refs', price: v1.price, std: ship_standard_id, express: ship_express_id, nwd: ship_next_id, std_free: ship_standard_free_id, nwd_free: ship_next_free_id %},
            "hasMerchantReturnPolicy": { "@id": {{ return_id | json }} }
          }
        ]
      }
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- when 'collection' -%},
      {%- comment -%}
        ItemList carries a full `item` per entry, not a bare name+url. A ListItem with only a name
        is a link; a ListItem whose `item` is a Product with a price and an availability is an
        answerable fact, and that is the difference between being read and being cited.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {
        "@type": "ItemList",
        "@id": {{ page_url | append: '#itemlist' | json }},
        "name": {{ collection.title | json }},
        "numberOfItems": {{ collection.all_products_count }},
        "itemListOrder": "https://schema.org/ItemListOrderAscending",
        "itemListElement": [
          {%- for prod in collection.products limit: 48 -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign pv = prod.selected_or_first_available_variant | default: prod.variants.first
            comment
              300, not the 1200 the PDP node uses. A listing entry is a summary, and a collection
              can carry 48 of them — at 1200 the two 16-product collections would add ~19KB of
              duplicated body copy to the head. 300 is a full opening sentence, which is what
              Google's "description" wants here, and it is the same source text either way.
            endcomment
            assign pdesc = prod.description | strip_html | strip_newlines
            capture pdesc
              render 'senseless-jsonld-text', text: pdesc
            endcapture
            assign pdesc = pdesc | truncate: 300
            if pdesc == blank
              assign pdesc = prod.title | append: ' — a topical cosmetic preparation by Senseless.'
            endif
          -%}
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": {{ forloop.index }},
            "name": {{ prod.title | json }},
            "url": {{ base | append: prod.url | json }},
            "item": {
              "@type": "Product",
              "@id": {{ base | append: prod.url | append: '#product' | json }},
              "name": {{ prod.title | json }},
              "description": {{ pdesc | json }},
              "url": {{ base | append: prod.url | json }},
              {%- if prod.featured_image -%}"image": {{ prod.featured_image | image_url: width: 800 | prepend: 'https:' | json }},{%- endif -%}
              {%- if pv.sku != blank -%}"sku": {{ pv.sku | json }},{%- endif -%}
              "brand": { "@type": "Brand", "name": {{ seller_name | json }} },
              "offers": {
                "@type": "Offer",
                "price": "{{ prod.price | divided_by: 100.0 }}",
                "priceCurrency": {{ cur | json }},
                "availability": "https://schema.org/{% if prod.available %}InStock{% else %}OutOfStock{% endif %}",
                "url": {{ base | append: prod.url | json }},
                "seller": { "@id": {{ org_id | json }} },
                "itemCondition": "https://schema.org/NewCondition",
                "shippingDetails": {% render 'senseless-shipping-refs', price: prod.price, std: ship_standard_id, express: ship_express_id, nwd: ship_next_id, std_free: ship_standard_free_id, nwd_free: ship_next_free_id %},
                "hasMerchantReturnPolicy": { "@id": {{ return_id | json }} }
              }
            }
          }{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        ]
      }

    {%- endcase -%}
  ]
}
</script>
